title The program written down
prompt Keaton: a single sitting's grant covering eight laps, closing -- I grant all of this and all your recommendations, publish seed when you're all done.
think A grant this wide is a program rather than a lap, and two laps of it have landed. Writing the remaining six down is the captain's job: a peer ship can then claim one under claim-as-override without re-deriving a shape I have already measured.
think Each open lap carries what the survey and the two landed laps already taught it. Lap C knows its five literals by count. Lap D knows the sweep is whole-tree by law. Lap E knows its crux is one document booked twice. Lap F knows lap B is what made it checkable. Lap H knows the answer it must NOT assume.
think The publish waits, and the reason is the program rather than caution. Laps C through H rewrite the seed's own front door, its onboarding guide and its contributing grammar; a seed published between them teaches a newcomer the world we are in the middle of leaving. publish-seed.sh in its bare form already encodes exactly this -- it projects, proves, commits, and stops.
obs THE CARD HAD 411 BYTES AND THE BOOKING WANTED 460. Three trims later it fits at 40,948 of 40,960 -- twelve bytes free. That is a pin telling me its next lap, and it is the same sentence the baton already says: a living pin at its ceiling taxes every lap a judgment call.
obs A GRADE BELOW B PUSHED A FRAME AND THE FRAME CLOSED WITH A REWRITE. The program page first read register 65 -- 35% negative sentences against Field's 30% ceiling -- so twelve sentences were restated to lead with what is. Register 93, composite 95. The discipline works exactly as written: touch it, read it, grade it, and let the grade decide.
obs LAP H IS THE ONE I MUST NOT ANSWER FROM THE ASK. Keaton granted the context-to-foundations alias if I recommend it. alias-sameness seats one referent, one implementation, and PEERS -- so a hundred duplicated pages would be a second copy wearing a synonym's clothes, the exact fault that rule prevents. The lap's job is to test that reading against the room, and a recommendation written before the reading would be a preference wearing a measurement's clothes.
